---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import { ORG } from '../../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Make a Donation"
  description="Donate to the Florida Lantern Project. A 501(c)(3) public charity, EIN 86-3574323."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="One-time gift"
    title="Hurricane season doesn't wait for our fundraising calendar"
    lede="Gifts made now are what's available when the next storm forms — not the next time we hold an event."
  >
    <p class="actions"><a class="btn" href={ORG.social.givebutter}>Donate now</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <Section title="What your gift does">
    <p class="intro">
      In 2024 we assisted more than 50 individuals and families through Hurricanes
      Helene and Milton on an operating budget of nothing at all — hotel rooms
      negotiated, a drone, volunteers, and partners who said yes.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is not a sustainable way to run a disaster response, and it is why we
      ask. Every dollar shortens the distance between a family calling and someone
      being able to say yes.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/response">See what we did &rarr;</a></p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="Giving monthly goes further">
    <p>
      If you're weighing a one-time gift against the same amount spread across a
      year, the monthly version is materially more useful to us — it's the reserve
      that lets us book a hotel room the night before landfall.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/give/lantern-keeper">About Lantern Keepers</a></p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Tax information">
    <p>
      {ORG.legalName} is a 501(c)(3) public charity. EIN <strong>{ORG.ein}</strong>.
      Donations are tax-deductible to the extent allowed by law, and you'll receive
      a receipt by email.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/about/transparency">Full transparency and financial information &rarr;</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .actions { margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .intro { font-size: var(--step-1); }
</style>
